e about his tobacco use was honest.\n\nFamily History\n\nHis mother had hypertension, which began at the age of 78. She passed away, but the exact age at death is not known.\n\nConclusion\n\nMr. Bass has been managing his alcohol use disorder effectively, with a notable history of sobriety. His recent visits have shown stable blood pressure and weight, with no major health concerns aside from the back strain and URI mentioned above. His social history includes a past smoking habit that he has successfully quit. His family history is significant for hypertension in his mother.\n\nPlease let me know if you require any further informatio"
